{
    "background_story": "Edgar was a renowned entomologist with a passion for the often-overlooked order of Hemiptera, commonly known as true bugs. His fascination with these insects began during his childhood, spent exploring the woods behind his family's rural home. As he delved deeper into the world of Hemiptera, Edgar became particularly interested in the unique characteristics of these bugs, such as their piercing-sucking mouthparts and diverse range of species. His groundbreaking research on the evolutionary adaptations of Hemiptera earned him international recognition, and he was soon invited to lead expeditions to remote regions in search of new species. Edgar's dedication to the study of Hemiptera led to the discovery of several previously unknown species, cementing his legacy as a leading expert in the field.",
